---
import Bento from "./Bento.astro";
import Demo from "./Demo.astro";
import Dither from "./Dither.astro";
---

<section id="everything" class="section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 class="heading-4 md:heading-2 reveal">The rest of the notebook</h2>
    <div class="clip reveal">
      <Demo
        name="tour"
        alt="A tour of Logia. In a note, the slash menu adds a heading, a checklist and a table. Then a note opens with its outline, links and backlinks, a backlink is followed, today's note opens with Ctrl Shift D, shapes and arrows are drawn on a canvas, and a task is added and moved on the task board."
      />
    </div>
    <Bento />

    <div class="yours card reveal">
      <Dither x={1} y={0} spread={0.35} />
      <div>
        <h2 class="heading-5 md:heading-3">Plain files. Your Git. Your keys.</h2>
        <p class="body-3 muted lede">
          Every note is a JSON file in <code>~/Documents/Logia</code>. Sync is plain Git, to a private remote you pick, over your own
          SSH keys. API keys sit in your OS keychain, and deleted notes wait 14 days in the trash before they go.
        </p>
      </div>
      <p class="early body-6 muted">
        <b>Heads up: it's early.</b> Logia began as one person's tool, so expect rough edges. There's no Mac on the desk to test
        with, so macOS gets the least attention.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .clip {
    margin-top: var(--s-400);
  }

  .yours {
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--s-300);
    margin-top: var(--s-200);
    padding: var(--s-300);
    background: var(--bg-warm);
  }

  .yours > :not(canvas) {
    position: relative;
  }

  .lede {
    margin-top: var(--s-100);
    max-width: 680px;
  }

  code {
    color: var(--ink-100);
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  .early b {
    color: var(--ember-300);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  @media (min-width: 1000px) {
    .yours {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 2fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: var(--s-700);
      align-items: end;
      padding: var(--s-500);
    }
  }
</style>
